# Journal - Sept 5 - Spark


## Today in one sentence
- Learned about data quality validation, presented our end-to-end Instacart pipeline to the team, and got introduced to Spark SQL and PySpark.

## What I learned
- Learned about data quality validation, including why it matters to check data at each step of a pipeline rather than only at the very end.
- Got to discuss and present our end-to-end pipeline for Instacart as a team, which helped clarify how each part of the project connects to the others.
- Spark SQL and PySpark were also discussed, giving a first look at how these tools are used to process larger datasets compared to regular SQL or pandas.

## Terms I am still learning
- Spark SQL - a way to write SQL-style queries that run on Spark, which is built to handle large amounts of data
- PySpark - the Python interface for using Spark, letting you write Spark code in Python instead of Scala

## What confused me
- At first, Spark felt confusing because it processes data differently from tools I'm used to, and I'm still getting a feel for how it splits and handles data behind the scenes.

